<p class="lt-chem-1155">1) Form enolate</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-1155"><img alt="" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," style="" /></p>

<p class="lt-chem-1155">2) Form enone</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-1155"><img alt="" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," style="" /></p>

<p class="lt-chem-1155">When performing both reactions together always consider the aldol product first then convert to the enone. Note! The double bond always forms in conjugation with the carbonyl.</p>

